  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSOLIDATING A HEMISPHERIC PLAN FOR THE ATLANTIC FLYWAY</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will finalize the development of a second phase business plan by 1) engaging Latin American stakeholders in refining the conceptual model, 2) identifying and prioritizing strategies and projects, and 3) aligning the plan with existing national and regional plans, with the long-term goal of creating a platform for the recovery of shorebird populations within the Atlantic Flyway, that by 2025 1) Maintains or increases both the extent and values of shorebird habitat compared to 2015, and 2) Increases target shorebird populations by 10%. This will be achieved by holding a series of meetings with key stakeholders in the Caribbean and South America to revise the current conceptual model, incorporating strategies and activities identified by stakeholders; building a broad hemispheric partnership of partners actively engaged in the development and implementation of the business plan; and, integrate the business plan with existing national, regional and species-specific shorebird conservation plans.</narrative>
  </description>
